      role: 'Keyboard scan, joysticks, cassette, interrupts and interval timer, over the CRU serial bus.',
      pkg: 'DIP-40', machines: ['ti994a', 'ti994'], location: { ti994a: 'U300' },
      summary: 'The PSI talks to the 9900 over the CRU (pins 2-4, enable on pin 5); S0-S4 (pins 39, 36, 35, 25, 24) are inputs that take the CRU bit address from A10-A14, they are not keyboard drivers. On the TI, P2-P4 select a keyboard column or joystick through a decoder, and the keys and joystick switches come back on the interrupt inputs INT3-INT10. P5 is ALPHA LOCK, P6 and P7 the cassette motors, P8 audio gate, P9 cassette out, P11 cassette in. INT1 is the I/O port interrupt and INT2 the VDP frame interrupt. A dead key row, no cassette or stuck interrupts point here.',
