  symptoms: {
    ti994a: [
      { symptom: 'Power LED off, nothing works', suspects: [], note: 'Check the transformer first: AC on pins 1-2 and 2-4 of the 4-pin plug. Then the regulator board: +12 V (7812, U1), -5 V (79M05, U2), +5 V (723 switcher). TI guide: unplug the supply from the logic board and recheck; if the rails come back, look for a short on the board.' },
      { symptom: 'No title screen', suspects: ['tms9900', 'tms9904', 'sram6810', 'romconsole'], note: 'Check the -5 V, +5 V and +12 V rails first, then the 9900 clocks (pins 8, 9, 25, 28) and /RESET on pin 6. Then READY on pin 62 (must not be stuck low), the scratchpad RAM and the console ROMs.' },
      { symptom: 'Dead console, no title screen', suspects: ['tms9900', 'tms9904'], note: 'The 9900 and its clock. The TI debug list checks all three rails and the four 12 V clocks from the TIM9904 first.' },
      { symptom: 'No picture, or garbled picture', suspects: ['vdp9918', 'dram4116'], note: 'The 9918A and its eight 4116 VRAM chips (U102-U109). Check pin 38 for 3.579545 MHz, then the /CSR and /CSW strobes on pins 15 and 14, then 4116 data out on pin 14. A lost -5 V rail kills 4116s.' },
      { symptom: 'Bad colour', suspects: ['vdp9918'], note: 'TI says adjust the VDP crystal (L100) so pin 38 reads 3.579545 MHz; the system tolerates 3.579520 to 3.579548 MHz.' },
      { symptom: 'Dead keys or a dead key row', suspects: ['tms9901'], note: 'Keyboard lines come into the 9901 interrupt inputs; P2-P4 select the column. A whole dead row is one 9901 line or the decoder.' },
      { symptom: 'No cassette, or stuck interrupts', suspects: ['tms9901'], note: 'The 9901 handles the cassette lines (P6-P9, P11) and the interrupt inputs. Sams: if CS1 will not run, check Q401 emitter-collector resistance (low when the motor should run).' },
      { symptom: 'No sound, or distorted sound', suspects: ['psg76489'], note: 'Check +5 V on pin 16 and the clock on pin 14 (447 kHz on an SN94624, 3.58 MHz on an SN76489).' },
      { symptom: 'Won\'t boot, or garbled graphics', suspects: ['grom0430', 'romconsole'], note: 'GROMs are a TI quirk. Check GROM select (pin 10), ready (pin 15) and clock (pin 13) before you swap the 9900. Sams: blank screen = try GROM U500; "insert cartridge" after pressing 1 = U501; no line feed on ENTER = U502.' },
    ],
  },
